    <text>
        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="grc">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><persName type="attested" key="Diadoumenos"><name nymRef="Διαδούμενος">Διαδούμε-
                    <lb n="2" break="no"/>νος</name></persName> ἑαυτῷ καὶ
                    <lb n="3"/><persName type="attested" key="Heliade"><name nymRef="Ηλιάς">Ἡλιάδι</name></persName> τῇ συνβ[ί-]
                    <lb n="4"/>ῳ τὸν βωμὸν
                    <lb n="5"/>καὶ τὴν στήλην
                    <lb n="6"/>καὶ τὰ πέλτα, καὶ
                    <lb n="7"/>ἐνορκῶ τρῖς θ[εοὺς]
                    <lb n="8"/><persName type="divine" key="Men"><name nymRef="Μήν">Μήνας</name></persName> ἀνεπιλύ[τως]
                    <lb n="9"/>μηδένα ἕτερον ἐ-
                    <lb n="10" break="no"/>πεισενεχθῆναι ἢ
                    <lb n="11"/>μόνην <persName type="attested" key="Artemeisia"><name nymRef="Αρτεμεισία">Ἀρτεμεισίαν</name></persName> τὴν
                    <lb n="12"/>ἐμήν.
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus"/>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="it"><p>DA_COMPILARE</p></div>
            <div type="commentary"><p>Il testo invoca "τρεῖς θεοὺς Μήνας" (r. 7-8), letteralmente "tre dèi Men": una forma plurale/triadica del dio non altrimenti specificata da epiteti distintivi in questo passo, marcata con un unico persName data l'assenza di elementi testuali per distinguere le tre manifestazioni.</p></div>
